.TH "GIT-WORK" "1" "Apr 2019" "Generated from git-work's source code" ""

.SH NAME
git-work-user - List identities, one line each


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgit-work user [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
List the identities this repository knows about, one line per identity:
the id and the display name.

.PP
This is the human form of \fBgit work user list\fR, which prints the same
identities as JSON and is the form to script against; --format json prints
that here too.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-f\fP, \fB--format\fP="text"
	Select the output formatting style. Valid values are [text,json]

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for user


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBgit-work(1)\fP, \fBgit-work-user-adopt(1)\fP, \fBgit-work-user-list(1)\fP, \fBgit-work-user-me(1)\fP, \fBgit-work-user-new(1)\fP
